***************************** T A L Y S **************************8234 1451  181
                                                                  8234 1451  182
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   8234 1451  183
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      8234 1451  184
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    8234 1451  185
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     8234 1451  186
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  8234 1451  187
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        8234 1451  188
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    8234 1451  189
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         8234 1451  190
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      8234 1451  191
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    8234 1451  192
stored in this data file:                                         8234 1451  193
                                                                  8234 1451  194
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   8234 1451  195
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     8234 1451  196
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 8234 1451  197
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   8234 1451  198
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                8234 1451  199
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   8234 1451  200
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    8234 1451  201
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        8234 1451  202
- Recoil data                                                     8234 1451  203
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           8234 1451  204
- Total particle energy spectra                                   8234 1451  205
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      8234 1451  206
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        8234 1451  207
- Residual production cross sections                              8234 1451  208
                                                                  8234 1451  209
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            8234 1451  210
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        8234 1451  211
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   8234 1451  212
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                8234 1451  213
                                                                  8234 1451  214
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************8234 1451  215
