##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    8234 1451  217
                                                                  8234 1451  218
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       8234 1451  219
                                                                  8234 1451  220
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          8234 1451  221
                                                                  8234 1451  222
##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   8234 1451  223
                                                                  8234 1451  224
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 8234 1451  225
                                                                  8234 1451  226
Details about the origin of the resonance parameters for this     8234 1451  227
nuclide are given above in this description. In general, both a   8234 1451  228
Resolved and an Unresolved Resonance Range are given.             8234 1451  229
                                                                  8234 1451  230
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                8234 1451  231
                                                                  8234 1451  232
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       8234 1451  233
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  8234 1451  234
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   8234 1451  235
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  8234 1451  236
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  8234 1451  237
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 8234 1451  238
to the highest incident energy.                                   8234 1451  239
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:8234 1451  240
                                                                  8234 1451  241
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  8234 1451  242
                                                                  8234 1451  243
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range,    8234 1451  244
or partly reproduced using experimental data.                     8234 1451  245
                                                                  8234 1451  246
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     8234 1451  247
                                                                  8234 1451  248
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    8234 1451  249
total cross section.                                              8234 1451  250
                                                                  8234 1451  251
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            8234 1451  252
                                                                  8234 1451  253
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    8234 1451  254
                                                                  8234 1451  255
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        8234 1451  256
                                                                  8234 1451  257
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  8234 1451  258
                                                                  8234 1451  259
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           8234 1451  260
                                                                  8234 1451  261
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   8234 1451  262
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        8234 1451  263
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     8234 1451  264
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         8234 1451  265
sections.                                                         8234 1451  266
                                                                  8234 1451  267
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 8234 1451  268
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 8234 1451  269
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 8234 1451  270
- MT28     : (n,np) cross section                                 8234 1451  271
- MT51-90  : (n,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      8234 1451  272
- MT91     : (n,n') continuum cross section                       8234 1451  273
- MT102    : (n,gamma) cross section                              8234 1451  274
- MT103    : (n,p) cross section                                  8234 1451  275
- MT104    : (n,d) cross section                                  8234 1451  276
- MT105    : (n,t) cross section                                  8234 1451  277
- MT106    : (n,h) cross section                                  8234 1451  278
- MT107    : (n,a) cross section                                  8234 1451  279
- MT600-610: (n,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       8234 1451  280
- MT649    : (n,p) continuum cross section                        8234 1451  281
- MT650-655: (n,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        8234 1451  282
- MT699    : (n,d) continuum cross section                        8234 1451  283
- MT700-705: (n,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        8234 1451  284
- MT749    : (n,t) continuum cross section                        8234 1451  285
- MT750-755: (n,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        8234 1451  286
- MT799    : (n,h) continuum cross section                        8234 1451  287
- MT800-810: (n,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       8234 1451  288
- MT849    : (n,a) continuum cross section                        8234 1451  289
                                                                  8234 1451  290
##### MF4: ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES           8234 1451  291
                                                                  8234 1451  292
We use MF4 for the neutron scattering angular distribution for    8234 1451  293
discrete levels.                                                  8234 1451  294
                                                                  8234 1451  295
- MT2      : Elastic angular distribution                         8234 1451  296
                                                                  8234 1451  297
The flag LTT=3 is used to indicate a switch at some high energy,  8234 1451  298
generally 50 MeV, from a Legendre representation to a tabulated   8234 1451  299
representation. For incident energies below this energy, the      8234 1451  300
Legendre coefficients are given on a sufficiently precise energy  8234 1451  301
grid. They are a sum of calculated Legendre coefficients for      8234 1451  302
compound nucleus and shape-elastic scattering. For higher         8234 1451  303
incident energies, relative angular distributions are tabulated   8234 1451  304
on an angular grid.                                               8234 1451  305
                                                                  8234 1451  306
- MT51-70  : (n,n') angular distribution for 1st-20th state       8234 1451  307
- MT600-610: (n,p) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        8234 1451  308
- MT650-655: (n,d) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         8234 1451  309
- MT700-705: (n,t) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         8234 1451  310
- MT750-755: (n,h) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         8234 1451  311
- MT800-810: (n,a) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        8234 1451  312
                                                                  8234 1451  313
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     8234 1451  314
                                                                  8234 1451  315
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     8234 1451  316
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   8234 1451  317
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  8234 1451  318
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             8234 1451  319
All data are generated with TALYS.                                8234 1451  320
                                                                  8234 1451  321
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   8234 1451  322
                                                                  8234 1451  323
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      8234 1451  324
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   8234 1451  325
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   8234 1451  326
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are8234 1451  327
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   8234 1451  328
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  8234 1451  329
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              8234 1451  330
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 8234 1451  331
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  8234 1451  332
For each residual product:                                        8234 1451  333
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               8234 1451  334
- the recoil                                                      8234 1451  335
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         8234 1451  336
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     8234 1451  337
sections.                                                         8234 1451  338
                                                                  8234 1451  339
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     8234 1451  340
                                                                  8234 1451  341
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  8234 1451  342
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 8234 1451  343
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          8234 1451  344
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       8234 1451  345
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 8234 1451  346
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     8234 1451  347
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  8234 1451  348
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      8234 1451  349
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         8234 1451  350
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             8234 1451  351
                                                                  8234 1451  352
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   8234 1451  353
followed:                                                         8234 1451  354
                                                                  8234 1451  355
- MT17 : (n,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         8234 1451  356
- MT22 : (n,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         8234 1451  357
- MT28 : (n,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         8234 1451  358
- MT91 : (n,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     8234 1451  359
- MT649: (n,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     8234 1451  360
- MT699: (n,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     8234 1451  361
- MT749: (n,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     8234 1451  362
- MT809: (n,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     8234 1451  363
- MT849: (n,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     8234 1451  364
                                                                  8234 1451  365
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 8234 1451  366
                                                                  8234 1451  367
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    8234 1451  368
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          8234 1451  369
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     8234 1451  370
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          8234 1451  371
                                                                  8234 1451  372
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  8234 1451  373
                                                                  8234 1451  374
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     8234 1451  375
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    8234 1451  376
as isomer.                                                        8234 1451  377
                                                                  8234 1451  378
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 8234 1451  379
                                                                  8234 1451  380
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        8234 1451  381
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    8234 1451  382
as isomer.                                                        8234 1451  383
                                                                  8234 1451  384
##### MF12: PHOTON PRODUCTION YIELD DATA                          8234 1451  385
                                                                  8234 1451  386
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:8234 1451  387
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   8234 1451  388
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   8234 1451  389
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   8234 1451  390
  given                                                           8234 1451  391
                                                                  8234 1451  392
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          8234 1451  393
                                                                  8234 1451  394
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  8234 1451  395
                                                                  8234 1451  396
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 8234 1451  397
                                                                  8234 1451  398
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         8234 1451  399
                                                                  8234 1451  400
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   8234 1451  401
                                                                  8234 1451  402
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters,        8234 1451  403
and more details are given above in this description. In most     8234 1451  404
versions of TENDL, this information is now stored in MF33.        8234 1451  405
                                                                  8234 1451  406
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 8234 1451  407
                                                                  8234 1451  408
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  8234 1451  409
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     8234 1451  410
with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates TALYS runs using    8234 1451  411
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   8234 1451  412
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  8234 1451  413
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                8234 1451  414
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      8234 1451  415
   same reaction channel between different energies)              8234 1451  416
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      8234 1451  417
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               8234 1451  418
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      8234 1451  419
   different reaction channels for different energies)            8234 1451  420
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        8234 1451  421
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              8234 1451  422
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  8234 1451  423
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       8234 1451  424
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     8234 1451  425
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  8234 1451  426
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     8234 1451  427
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     8234 1451  428
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     8234 1451  429
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   8234 1451  430
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   8234 1451  431
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  8234 1451  432
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   8234 1451  433
                                                                  8234 1451  434
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  8234 1451  435
                                                                  8234 1451  436
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       8234 1451  437
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  8234 1451  438
are generated with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates       8234 1451  439
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   8234 1451  440
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         8234 1451  441
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  8234 1451  442
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      8234 1451  443
representation is used.                                           8234 1451  444
                                                                  8234 1451  445
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      8234 1451  446
                                                                  8234 1451  447
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  8234 1451  448
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             8234 1451  449
                                                                  8234 1451  450
